.TITLE "cd"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the current working directory. It updates the shell environment to a new path, allowing you to navigate the filesystem.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**chdir**

.DIV "TLDR"
**cd path/to/directory**
Changes the current working directory to the specified path.
> __path/to/directory__ the target folder path

**cd ..**
Moves the current working directory up one level to the parent folder.
> 

**cd**
Returns the user to their home directory.
> 

**cd -**
Switches the current working directory back to the previous path.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Running __cd__ without any arguments is the fastest way to return to your home directory. Use it frequently alongside __pwd__ to maintain awareness of your location in the filesystem.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ls** **mac:pwd**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/cd.html__
